  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Detyens Shipyards has $261M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, spread across 22 awards with an average award size of $11.9M. Obligations are up 9.4% year over year. The Department of Defense bought the most, obligating $204M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $42.1M and the Department of Commerce at $14.9M. Historical obligations by fiscal year show $96.5M in FY21, $143M in FY22, $91.7M in FY23, $121M in FY24, $239M in FY25, and $261M in FY26. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date), and the figures presented are contract obligations except where tables note award-value as total contract values. These numbers summarize federal buying of Detyens Shipyards through FY2026 to date, highlight agency concentration in the Department of Defense, and show year-to-date growth relative to the prior year.",
